# What the tests read. Copy this file to `.env.test`, which git ignores, and fill in the services
# you want them to meet for real. A service left as it is keeps its fake.
#
# Bun loads this file into every `bun test`, so it holds the default for every run. A credential
# alone changes nothing: each service has one variable that says which of the two a run wants, and
# one run can say otherwise without the file being touched:
#
#   HCLOUD_MODE=real bun test tests/convex/allocations   meets Hetzner, for that run
#   CLERK_MODE=real bun test tests/convex/clerk.test.ts  meets Clerk, for that run
#   HCLOUD_MODE=fake bun test                            keeps the fake, whatever the file says
#
# See `docs/setups/hetzner-cloud.md`. The project a run meets must hold nothing else: it makes its
# own firewall, labels everything it creates, removes all of it at the end, and removes what a
# killed run left behind, so anything still in that project afterwards is a leak.
HCLOUD_MODE=fake
HCLOUD_TOKEN=

# See `docs/setups/clerk.md`. An instance of its own, because a run makes accounts and deletes
# them, and a development instance holds a hundred. The Frontend API URL is the issuer the
# deployment trusts, so a run that meets Clerk signs in with tokens Clerk itself signed.
CLERK_MODE=fake
CLERK_FRONTEND_API_URL=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
